16. Practical Research Workflow
1. Understand the business and its industry.
2. Collect annual reports and financial statements.
3. Analyze revenue, profitability, cash flow and debt.
4. Evaluate management and governance.
5. Compare the company with peers.
6. Build financial forecasts.
7. Estimate intrinsic value using appropriate valuation methods.
8. Run sensitivity and downside scenarios.
9. Define the investment thesis and risks.
10. Document the decision and monitor new information.
